From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fan: log unmatched scanned inputs at debug level

The fan scanner enumerates hwmon inputs that may belong to other sensor
services or have no Entity-Manager configuration yet. Skipping such inputs
is expected during discovery. Keep real configuration and read failures at
error level, without changing sensor selection or retry behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
+++ b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
@@ -397,8 +397,8 @@
             if (sensorData == nullptr)
             {
-                lg2::error("failed to find match for '{PATH}'", "PATH",
-                           path.string());
+                lg2::debug("Skipping unmatched fan input '{PATH}'", "PATH",
+                           path.string());
                 continue;
             }
 
             auto findSensorName = baseConfiguration->second.find("Name");
